CPython
=======

These builtins are ports of code of CPython 3.13:

- `src/div.rs` ports `_float_div_mod` and `float_rem` of
  `Objects/floatobject.c`.
- `src/round.rs` ports `double_round` of `Objects/floatobject.c`.
- `src/gamma.rs` ports `m_tgamma` and `m_lgamma` of
  `Modules/mathmodule.c`.
- `src/hypot.rs` ports `math_hypot` and `vector_norm` of
  `Modules/mathmodule.c`, for two numbers.
- `src/math.rs` ports `math_ulp` and `m_remainder`, and `src/pow.rs`
  ports `math_pow`, of `Modules/mathmodule.c`.

The ports are in Rust and work on `f64` alone. Where CPython raises an
exception, they return a value that the emitted code turns into the same
exception. `src/round.rs` computes the digits with its own exact
arithmetic, in place of the `dtoa` of CPython. `src/gamma.rs` calls the
`exp`, `log` and `pow` of this crate and the `sin` and `cos` of the `libm`
crate, in place of the libm of the system.

